WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:07.940
Before we get started, if you have any questions
about the upcoming IT movie, stick around

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.010
to the end of this video to find out how you
can get answers.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:14.500
When we did the 19 Things You Want To See
In The Shining at Halloween Horror Nights,

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.010
some of you guys were also curious about what
we could come up with for a Stephen King’s

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:22.051
IT Themed Maze, and since there are still
unannounced attractions, we decided to come

00:00:22.051 --> 00:00:23.990
up with our own version.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.900
If they were to do a haunt based on the property,
they would most definitely base it off the

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.679
upcoming IT movie coming out in September.

00:00:30.679 --> 00:00:36.510
But since that movie isn’t out yet, we’ll
be basing our ideas mostly off of the 1990

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:40.760
mini-series starring Tim Curry and Stephen
King’s original novel, in addition to what

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:42.700
we know about this new movie.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:46.230
We decided that the best haunted house they
can create around this franchise would have

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:49.850
to be centered around the Lucky 7’s descent
into the Derry sewers.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:53.470
We can imagine theme park guests lining up
in “The Barrens” with the creepy sewer

00:00:53.470 --> 00:00:55.699
entrance building looming in the distance.

00:00:55.699 --> 00:00:59.739
The design of this queue could take some inspiration
from what B&amp;M did with the entrance to Batman

00:00:59.739 --> 00:01:03.890
the Ride, where guests wait in line from the
nice part of town, to the slums and eventually

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:06.370
into the sewer drain pipe just before getting
on the ride.

00:01:06.370 --> 00:01:10.370
They use dark eerie paths through the pipes
in combination with sound effects to give

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:14.500
the impression of water dripping and huge
industrial fans blowing in order to build

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.550
tension before reaching the ride.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:19.990
They also use realistic looking signage to
make the guests feel like they are entering

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:22.040
somewhere they aren’t supposed to be.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:25.250
These elements could all be used in order
to put people on edge during their approach

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.909
to Derry’s sewers.

00:01:26.909 --> 00:01:31.750
Once guests are in the sewer, they can use
the hallucinations Pennywise creates for his

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:36.760
victims to frighten guests and show off the
iconic scenes from within the sewers.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:40.760
The Deadlights, which are bright lights that
travel through the sewer pipes and are known

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:47.180
to be IT’s true form, can be used as transitions
to disorient patrons in between these hallucinations.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:51.549
This also gives a perfect opportunity for
the bullies or Pennywise to frighten guests

00:01:51.549 --> 00:01:54.150
at the beginning or end of each transition.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:57.530
And using this format will also allow the
creators to include all of our favorite moments

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:01.869
from the story that normally take place above
ground down in the sewers, just as we see

00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:05.490
at the end of the child arc, where Pennywise
uses different forms to try to trick the kids

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:06.649
into letting their guard down.

00:02:06.649 --> 00:02:09.630
Here are a few rooms that we’ve come up
with as an example.

00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:14.430
One room can feature sheets on a laundry line,
much like the death of Laurie Ann in the miniseries.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:18.630
There could be fans going to make these laundry
sheets flap around in the wind, allowing glimpses

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:22.830
of Pennywise to be seen behind some and not
behind others.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:25.960
This room is also a perfect environment for
jump scares with Pennywise.

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:30.500
While walking through the room, guests could
also see an occasional child singing “the

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:31.500
Itsy Bitsy Spider”.

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:35.750
There can be sound effects of an oncoming
storm paired with a slower rendition of the

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:38.360
rhyme; providing an uneasy experience for
guests.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:41.640
Another room could be a representation of
the storm scene.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:44.750
Since we are already in a sewer setting, it
makes sense that there would be metal grates

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:47.760
around anyways, leading to different lines
of the sewer.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.370
These would provide the opportunity for a
lot of sudden jump scares, similar in nature

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:54.470
to when Pennywise appears in the storm drain
to attack Georgie.

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:58.690
I think it would also be cool if the grates
that Pennywise is going to be appearing in

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:03.260
are loosely attached to give people the impression
that IT can bust right through and get them.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:07.090
Additionally the sound of metal clanking around
is oftentimes used for a startling effect

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:10.010
in the scare zones that we’ve attended in
previous years.

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:14.260
Universal loves it’s fog machines and misters,
so these can be used to create the illusion

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:18.560
of rain without actually getting the attendees
soaked, and they’ll also help keep our visibility

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:22.720
limited to what is directly in front us, setting
the stage for more scares.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:26.260
Not to mention that the Deadlights will look
reeealllllyyyy cool in the fog.

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:30.260
Taking place at Derry Elementary, the next
two rooms would be done in a pair.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:33.510
One being the shower scene where the shower
heads are moving on their own.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:37.540
Pennywise’s voice can be used to echo around
the room or sound like it’s coming from

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:38.540
the drain.

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:42.230
This has to be done in a relatively open room
where the pipes move and herd guests to a

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:43.550
small exit.

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:47.970
Fog used to imitate steam can be used as a
transition to a hallway where the bullies

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.040
are threatening Ben with a switchblade.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:54.700
Ben would be attempting to call for help from
the patrons, only to be ignored like various

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:58.160
other mazes such as, Krampus and Freddy vs
Jason.

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:02.970
The guest would then into the boiler room
and would encounter an iconic horror character,

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.840
just as Richie does in the book.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:10.550
Originally, he sees The Wolfman but if the
maze is based off the new movie, iconic 80s

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:15.670
characters like Freddy, Jason, Chucky, and
Zombies would be more likely.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:19.940
For the next area, I imagine guests continuing
down a long sewer pipe corridor.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:23.570
Nothing is popping out at them, creating an
uneasy calm.

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:28.330
As they go, ruined and bookshelves appear
on both sides and we gradually transition

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.900
into a library scene.

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:34.840
Just as the sewer grates provided a spot for
Pennywise pop up and scare us before, the

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:39.200
gaps in-between books on the shelves could
be used for a similar effect at the library.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:46.460
This would also be a good spot to incorporate
balloons and some of that creepy circus music.

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:50.180
Imagine walking through this library and you
hear the faint sound of circus music from

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:51.180
above.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:54.060
You look up and see a single red balloon floating
there.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.020
Then you hear Pennywise’s voice echo through
the corridor.

00:04:57.020 --> 00:04:58.950
“What’s the matter?

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:00.660
One balloon not enough?

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:02.610
TRY A BUNCH!”

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:06.480
And then a bunch of balloons on strings fall
down in front of you, just before Pennywise

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:09.640
comes charging through the sea of balloons
to come after you!

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:13.221
As people are making their way from room to
room, the one constant they always return

00:05:13.221 --> 00:05:18.940
to will be this central area, much how The
Exorcist maze in 2016 always returned to Regan’s

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:19.940
room.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:23.060
Everything we see will build up to that final
confrontation with Pennywise.

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:27.561
For the final showdown, they can recap all
the major set pieces using projections, as

00:05:27.561 --> 00:05:31.480
seen in the mini-seires when the Loser’s
Club goes down into the sewers as kids.

00:05:31.480 --> 00:05:35.780
This idea is actually pretty practical for
a theme park, considering we’ve seen something

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:38.770
similar in the new renovations on Pirates
of Caribbean.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:42.790
Finally, Pennywise can attack from behind
these mist walls and play on the suspense

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:45.120
of not knowing which one he is going to approach
from.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:49.030
The use of strobe lighting and sound effects
will make this the most intense part of the

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:50.030
walk through.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:54.900
I know a lot of you have questions for us
about the new IT movie, so here’s what we’re

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:55.900
going to do.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:06:01.730
Tweet your questions @CZsWorld_Horror and
use the #ITmovie and we’ll make a video

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:04.360
where we do our best to answer your questions.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:06.830
But you have to ask good questions.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:12.480
Yeah, if you ask us dumb questions like, “this
movie comes out on my birthday”, we won’t

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:13.570
address them.

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:16.620
Besides, for one, that’s not even a question.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:22.530
So go follow us @CZsWorld_Horror and if you
aren’t subscribed to the channel here, do

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:23.530
that as well.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:27.540
I make horrors in addition to talking about
them and I’ve got new videos for you every

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:32.639
week, so ring that death bell for notifications
and we’ll see you in the one.

00:06:32.639 --> 00:06:34.650
Assuming we both survive.

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:37.400
And we aaaalllll float.

